API/E2E Round 1 broader-validation setup adjustments

1. The first owned Docker attempt reached /rest/health and Chromium debug readiness, but direct invocation of the server's Electron-embedded open_tab adapter returned browser_unsupported_in_current_environment. This is the clean published Docker image's expected configuration: Docker/remote browser tools come from a user-configured BrowserServer MCP; the disposable data/workspace intentionally contained no user MCP checkout/config. The attempt's owned container and temp root were removed. The final run used the owned Docker Chromium CDP boundary to prove node-local URL ownership and records the BrowserServer MCP/provider path as not tested.

2. Project packaged Electron launch initially exited before readiness because the Codex host environment exported ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE=1 and the project launcher faithfully inherited sourceEnv. Evidence: 14a-electron-direct-launch.log (unsigned bundle plus inherited variable failed); 14c-electron-direct-launch-retry.log (locally ad-hoc-signed bundle plus inherited variable still failed); 14d-electron-direct-launch-clean-env.log (the same ad-hoc-signed bundle passed when invoked with env -u ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE). The final custom runner copied process.env then removed only this host-tool-only variable before calling the project E2E preparation API.

3. One invalid Playwright setup attempt terminated in Playwright before the custom finally block completed. Exact API/E2E-owned residue was then removed manually: Docker container autobyteus-api-e2e-open-tab-58069-1788066037242, temp Electron root autobyteus-e2e-koqN9A, and temp Docker root autobyteus-api-e2e-remote-SQRIUB. Pre-existing Aug-21 autobyteus-e2e roots were identified by timestamps and not touched. The final successful runner affirmatively removed its owned process group, data root, Docker container/root, and target server and showed unchanged production AutoByteus process and pre-existing container identity lists.

4. The local unsigned macOS app bundle was xattr-cleared and ad-hoc signed strictly for this runtime-validation run; 14b-electron-adhoc-sign.log records verification. The produced DMG/ZIP remained the original unsigned local build artifacts; 15-package-inspection.log records their hashes separately. No release/signing claim is made.
